:: OutOfLeads
<h2>Out of leads</h2>
<p class="quote chief">"That's all the time we have," your supervisor says. "What's your verdict?"</p>
<div class="actions"><<link "One last look at the deduction board">><<set $return to "OutOfLeads">><<goto "Board">><</link>>[[Give my verdict|Theories]]</div>


:: Beach
<h2>Tena Bar</h2>
<p>A wide, sandy beach on the Columbia River, cold wind off the water. The Ingram family shows you the shallow hole where Brian was smoothing out sand for a campfire. Agents with shovels and sifting screens are already combing the beach.</p>
<<clue "bundles">>
<<clue "place">>
<h3>Dig a test hole</h3>
<div id="dig"><<include "DigGrid">></div>
<<tomap>>


:: DigGrid
<<set _sq to [["nw","Up the beach, left"],["n","Up the beach"],["ne","Up the beach, right"],["w","Left of the hole"],["hole","Brian's hole"],["e","Right of the hole"],["sw","By the water, left"],["s","By the water"],["se","By the water, right"]]>>
<p class="meta"><<if $digsLeft gt 0>>You have time for <<print $digsLeft>> more <<print $digsLeft is 1 ? "hole" : "holes">>. Tap a square on the beach.<<else>>No time for more holes.<</if>></p>
<div class="dig-grid" role="group" aria-label="Beach squares">
<<for _d range _sq>><<capture _d>>
<<if $dug.includes(_d[0])>><span class="dig done"><<print _d[1]>><em><<if _d[0] is "w" or _d[0] is "e" or _d[0] is "hole">>Clay layer below the sand<<else>>Just sand<</if>></em></span>
<<elseif $digsLeft lte 0>><span class="dig off"><<print _d[1]>></span>
<<else>><span class="dig"><<link _d[1]>><<run $dug.push(_d[0])>><<set $digsLeft to $digsLeft - 1>><<replace "#dig">><<include "DigGrid">><</replace>><<if _d[0] is "w" or _d[0] is "e" or _d[0] is "hole">><<replace "#digresult">><<clue "trench">><</replace>><<run $(document).trigger(":interview-done")>><<else>><<replace "#digresult">><p class="note">Sand, sand and more sand. Nothing here.</p><</replace>><</if>><</link>></span><</if>>
<</capture>><</for>>
</div>
<div id="digresult" role="status"></div>


:: Lab
<h2>The FBI lab</h2>
<p>An agent lines the soggy bills up against a printout of the 1971 microfilm list, one serial number at a time.</p>
<p class="quote">"They match. This is the ransom. And look: the rubber bands are still on. Banks across the country have had this list for nine years, and not one of these bills has ever turned up anywhere else."</p>
<<clue "match">>
<<clue "banded">>
<<clue "unspent">>
<<tomap>>


:: Geologist
<h2>Interview: Leonard Palmer</h2>
<<include "Scene">>
<p>Leonard Palmer, a geologist from Portland State University, has dug careful trenches at Tena Bar and drawn the layers of sand like a cake.</p>
<div id="ans"><<pastanswers "palmer">></div>
<div id="iv"><<interview "palmer">></div>
<<tomap>>


:: RiverMap
<h2>The river map</h2>
<p>A big map of the Columbia River and the rivers that flow into it. Rivers carry things <b>downstream</b>, the way the arrows point. Tap each river to follow it.</p>
<figure class="rivermap">
<svg viewBox="0 0 360 300" role="img" aria-label="Map: the Columbia River flows west past Vancouver, then turns north. The Washougal joins it east of Vancouver, upstream of Tena Bar. Tena Bar is on the Columbia below the bend. The Lewis River, which runs past Ariel and Lake Merwin, joins the Columbia farther north, downstream of Tena Bar.">
<defs><marker id="arw" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="#2f5d8a"/></marker></defs>
