:: Weather
<h2>The weather bureau</h2>
<p>A clerk pulls the records for the night of November 24, 1971, along the flight path.</p>
<<clue "weather">>
<<clue "night">>
<<tomap>>


:: Files
<h2>The old 1971 search files</h2>
<p>Boxes of maps marked with grid squares. In 1971, searchers walked the forest near Ariel and Lake Merwin, square by square.</p>
<p class="quote">"Mud, steep hills, endless trees," an agent says. "No parachute. No money. No body."</p>
<<clue "nothing">>
<<clue "planner">>
<p>Clipped to the last box is a newer note.</p>
<<clue "placard">>
<<tomap>>


:: Newsroom
<h2>The newspaper office</h2>
<p>The Cooper story is back on every front page, and everyone has a theory.</p>
<p class="quote">"He's on a beach in Mexico, spending it," says one reporter. "No way," says another. "That beach is his grave."</p>
<<clue "rich">>
<<clue "dead">>
<<tomap>>


:: Theories [nobar]
<div class="stamp">Theory board</div>
<h2>How did the money get to Tena Bar?</h2>
<p>Four theories. For each one, decide: can your evidence <b>rule it out</b>, or is it <b>still possible</b>?</p>
<div id="thlist"><<include "TheoryList">></div>
<div id="thgo"><<include "TheoryGo">></div>


:: TheoryList
<<for _t range setup.theories>><<capture _t>>
<div class="sortrow"><p class="card-title"><<print _t.text>></p>
<div class="choices two"><<for _k range [["out","Ruled out"],["possible","Still possible"]]>><<capture _k>><span @class="$th[_t.id] is _k[0] ? 'opt chosen' : 'opt'"><<link _k[1]>><<set $th[_t.id] to _k[0]>><<replace "#thlist">><<include "TheoryList">><</replace>><<replace "#thgo">><<include "TheoryGo">><</replace>><</link>></span><</capture>><</for>></div></div>
<</capture>><</for>>


:: TheoryGo
<<if Object.keys($th).length lt setup.theories.length>><p class="note">Decide all four theories to go on.</p>
<<else>><div class="actions">[[On to my verdict|Accusation]]</div><</if>>


:: Accusation [nobar]
<div class="stamp">Verdict</div>
<h2>"Is Cooper alive or dead?"</h2>
<p class="quote chief">"Give me your verdict, how sure you are, and up to three cards that back it up."</p>
<h3>1. Your verdict</h3>
<div id="verdicts"><<include "VerdictList">></div>
<h3>2. How sure are you?</h3>
<div id="confs"><<include "ConfList">></div>
<h3>3. Pin up to 3 cards as evidence</h3>
<<if $notebook.length is 0>><p class="note">Your notebook is empty. You'll have to report with no evidence.</p>
<<else>><div id="pins"><<include "PinList">></div><</if>>
<div id="file"><<include "FileButton">></div>


:: VerdictList
<<set _opts to [["survived","He survived the jump"],["didnt","He didn't survive the jump"],["unknown","We can't tell yet"]]>>
<div class="choices"><<for _o range _opts>><<capture _o>><span @class="$verdict is _o[0] ? 'opt chosen' : 'opt'"><<link _o[1]>><<set $verdict to _o[0]>><<replace "#verdicts">><<include "VerdictList">><</replace>><<replace "#file">><<include "FileButton">><</replace>><</link>></span><</capture>><</for>></div>


:: ConfList
<<set _opts to [["hunch","Just a hunch"],["fairly","Fairly sure"],["very","Very sure"]]>>
<div class="choices"><<for _o range _opts>><<capture _o>><span @class="$conf is _o[0] ? 'opt chosen' : 'opt'"><<link _o[1]>><<set $conf to _o[0]>><<replace "#confs">><<include "ConfList">><</replace>><<replace "#file">><<include "FileButton">><</replace>><</link>></span><</capture>><</for>></div>


:: PinList
<p class="meta">Pinned: <<print $pinned.length>> of 3. Tap a card to pin or unpin it.</p>
<div class="cards pinboard">
<<for _id range $notebook>><<capture _id>><span @class="($pinned.includes(_id) ? 'opt pinned' : 'opt') + (setup.cards[_id].type === 'deduction' ? ' ded' : '')"><<link setup.cards[_id].title>><<if $pinned.includes(_id)>><<run $pinned.delete(_id)>><<elseif $pinned.length lt 3>><<run $pinned.push(_id)>><</if>><<replace "#pins">><<include "PinList">><</replace>><</link>></span><</capture>><</for>>
</div>


:: FileButton
<<if $verdict is "" or $conf is "">><p class="note">Choose a verdict and how sure you are to file your report.</p>
<<else>><div class="actions">[[File my verdict|Verdict]]</div><</if>>


:: Verdict [nobar]
<<set _lean to function(id){ var c = setup.cards[id]; return c.type === "deduction" ? c.leans : c.type; }>>
<<set _pins to $pinned.map(_lean)>>
<<set _nS to _pins.filter(function(x){ return x === "survived"; }).length>>
<<set _nD to _pins.filter(function(x){ return x === "didnt"; }).length>>
<<set _nA to _pins.filter(function(x){ return x === "assumption"; }).length>>
<<set _nb to $notebook.map(_lean)>>
<<set _haveS to _nb.includes("survived")>>
<<set _haveD to _nb.includes("didnt")>>
<<if $verdict is "survived">><<set _s1 to _nS gte 2 and _nA is 0>>
<<elseif $verdict is "didnt">><<set _s1 to _nD gte 2 and _nA is 0>>
<<else>><<set _s1 to _nS gte 1 and _nD gte 1 and _nA is 0>><</if>>
<<if $verdict is "unknown">><<set _s2 to $conf isnot "very">>
<<elseif $conf is "very">><<set _s2 to false>>
<<elseif $conf is "fairly">><<set _s2 to _s1>>
<<else>><<set _s2 to true>><</if>>
<<if $verdict is "survived">><<set _s3 to _haveD>><<elseif $verdict is "didnt">><<set _s3 to _haveS>><<else>><<set _s3 to _haveS and _haveD>><</if>>
<<set _thOk to setup.theories.map(function(t){ return $th[t.id] === t.answer && (t.answer !== "out" || t.needs.some(function(n){ return $notebook.includes(n); })); })>>
<<set _s4 to _thOk.every(function(x){ return x; })>>
<<set $stars to (_s1 ? 1 : 0) + (_s2 ? 1 : 0) + (_s3 ? 1 : 0) + (_s4 ? 1 : 0)>>
<<set $deductions to $notebook.filter(function(id){ return setup.cards[id].type === "deduction"; }).length>>
<<switch $verdict>>
<<case "survived">><div class="stamp">Verdict: survived</div>
<<case "didnt">><div class="stamp">Verdict: didn't survive</div>
<<default>><div class="stamp solved">Verdict: can't tell yet</div>
<</switch>>
<h2>So far: <<print $stars>> of 4 stars</h2>
<p class="meta">Nobody knows the true answer, so these stars measure how well you used evidence, not whether you "won." One more star waits in the suspect drawer.</p>
<ul class="stars">
<li @class="_s1 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print _s1 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>Evidence that fits your verdict.</b> <<if _s1>>The cards you pinned back up what you said.<<elseif _nA gt 0>>You pinned a newspaper guess. Guesses aren't evidence.<<elseif $verdict is "unknown">>For "can't tell yet," pin at least one card pointing each way.<<else>>Pin at least two cards that point toward your verdict.<</if>></li>
<li @class="_s2 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print _s2 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>Confidence that fits the evidence.</b> <<if $conf is "very" and $verdict isnot "unknown">>The evidence points both ways, so "very sure" is too sure.<<elseif $verdict is "unknown" and $conf is "very">>Very sure that nobody can tell? Fair, but "fairly sure" fits better.<<elseif _s2>>Your confidence matches how strong your evidence is.<<else>>"Fairly sure" needs pinned evidence that backs you up. Otherwise it's a hunch.<</if>></li>
<li @class="_s3 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print _s3 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>Looked at the other side.</b> <<if _s3>>You collected evidence pointing the other way, too.<<else>>You never found a clue pointing the other way. Good detectives look for evidence that could prove them wrong.<</if>></li>
<li @class="_s4 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print _s4 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>The theory board.</b> <<if _s4>>You ruled out three theories with evidence and kept the one nobody can rule out.<<else>>Here's how the evidence sorts them:<</if>></li>
</ul>
<<if not _s4>><ul class="theory-key"><<for _i to 0; _i lt setup.theories.length; _i++>><<set _t to setup.theories[_i]>><li @class="_thOk[_i] ? 'ok' : 'no'"><b><<print _t.text>>:</b> <<print _t.answer is "out" ? "ruled out" : "still possible">>. <<print _t.why>><<if _t.answer is "out" and $th[_t.id] is "out" and not _thOk[_i]>> (You didn't collect the clue that proves it.)<</if>></li><</for>></ul><</if>>
<p class="meta">Deductions worked out: <<print $deductions>> of <<print setup.dedTotal>></p>
<h3>Your notebook, flipped over</h3>
<<if $notebook.length is 0>><p class="note">You didn't collect any cards.</p><<else>>
<div class="cards reveal"><<for _id range $notebook>><<set _t to _lean(_id)>><div @class="'card ' + _t"><span class="tag"><<print setup.cards[_id].type === "deduction" ? "Deduction · " + setup.typeLabel[_t] : setup.typeLabel[_t]>></span><span class="card-title"><<print setup.cards[_id].title>></span><<if $pinned.includes(_id)>><span class="pinned-mark">You pinned this</span><</if>></div><</for>></div><</if>>
<div class="actions">[[Jump forward to today|Today]]</div>


:: Today [nobar]
<div class="stamp">Cold case room · today</div>
<h2>Today</h2>
<p>Fast-forward. You're in today's cold case room, and the Cooper file has grown to fill a whole wall. Science can now test things nobody could test in 1971.</p>
<<if $locker.includes("tie")>><div class="card"><span class="card-label">From your evidence locker</span><span class="card-title">The tie you bagged in 1971</span><span class="card-text">You bagged Cooper's clip-on tie in Part 1. Look what the lab found on it.</span></div>
<<else>><p class="note">You didn't bag the tie in Part 1, but luckily another agent did.</p><</if>>
<div class="card"><span class="card-label">Lab result, 2001</span><span class="card-title">DNA from the tie</span><span class="card-text">The FBI got a partial DNA profile from Cooper's tie. But it isn't a strong sample, and nobody knows if the tie was secondhand, so it might not be Cooper's DNA at all.</span></div>
<div class="card"><span class="card-label">Volunteer scientists, 2009 onward</span><span class="card-title">Specks of rare metal</span><span class="card-text">Under powerful microscopes, a volunteer team found tiny bits of rare metals on the tie, including pure titanium. In 1971, metals like that were used in only a few kinds of places, like aircraft factories.</span></div>
<<if $locker.includes("butts")>><div class="card"><span class="card-label">From your evidence locker</span><span class="card-title">The cigarette butts you bagged</span><span class="card-text">Bad news. The eight cigarette butts were destroyed in 1998 while in FBI storage. They might have held DNA. Lesson: evidence has to be protected, or it's gone forever.</span></div><</if>>
<<if $locker.includes("prints")>><div class="card"><span class="card-label">From your evidence locker</span><span class="card-title">The fingerprints you bagged</span><span class="card-text">Investigators lifted 66 fingerprints from the plane. Nobody has ever proven that any of them belonged to the hijacker.</span></div><</if>>
<p class="quote chief">"Over the years, investigators have looked at hundreds of suspects, more than 800 by many counts," says the agent on duty. "Here are five of the most famous. For each one, can the evidence rule him out?"</p>
<div class="actions">[[Open the suspect drawer|Suspects]]</div>


:: Suspects [nobar]
<h2>The suspect drawer</h2>
<p>Compare each suspect with the evidence: the description from two flight attendants (mid-forties, about 5 feet 10 to 6 feet, dark hair, brown eyes), the tie DNA, and any alibi. For each one, pick the evidence that matters most, then decide whether it rules him out.</p>
<p class="meta">Nobody knows who Cooper was. There's no right answer about guilt here. The star is for picking evidence that can actually be checked.</p>
<div id="suslist"><<include "SuspectList">></div>
<div id="susgo"><<include "SuspectGo">></div>


:: SuspectList
<<for _s range setup.suspects>><<capture _s>>
<div class="folder"><p class="folder-tab"><<print _s.name>></p>
<ul><<for _f range _s.facts>><li><<print _f>></li><</for>></ul>
<p class="poster-part">The evidence that matters most</p>
<div class="choices"><<for _ki, _kv range _s.keys>><<capture _ki, _kv>><span @class="$key[_s.id] === _ki ? 'opt chosen' : 'opt'"><<link _kv[0]>><<set $key[_s.id] to _ki>><<replace "#suslist">><<include "SuspectList">><</replace>><<replace "#susgo">><<include "SuspectGo">><</replace>><</link>></span><</capture>><</for>></div>
<p class="poster-part">Does it rule him out?</p>
<div class="choices two"><<for _k range [["out","Ruled out"],["possible","Can't rule out"]]>><<capture _k>><span @class="$sus[_s.id] is _k[0] ? 'opt chosen' : 'opt'"><<link _k[1]>><<set $sus[_s.id] to _k[0]>><<replace "#suslist">><<include "SuspectList">><</replace>><<replace "#susgo">><<include "SuspectGo">><</replace>><</link>></span><</capture>><</for>></div></div>
<</capture>><</for>>


:: SuspectGo
<<if Object.keys($sus).length lt setup.suspects.length or Object.keys($key).length lt setup.suspects.length>><p class="note">Pick the key evidence and decide for all five suspects to go on.</p>
<<else>><div class="actions">[[Close the drawer|SuspectResults]]</div><</if>>


:: SuspectResults [nobar]
<<set _ok to setup.suspects.map(function(s){ return s.keys[$key[s.id]][1]; })>>
<<set $s4 to _ok.every(function(x){ return x; })>>
<<set $stars to $stars + ($s4 ? 1 : 0)>>
<div @class="$s4 ? 'stamp solved' : 'stamp'">Suspects reviewed</div>
<h2>Detective rating: <<print $stars>> of 5 stars</h2>
<ul class="stars">
<li @class="$s4 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print $s4 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>Judging suspects by evidence.</b> <<if $s4>>For every suspect, you picked evidence that can actually be checked.<<else>>Some of your picks were things that can't be checked. See below.<</if>></li>
</ul>
<ul class="theory-key"><<for _i to 0; _i lt setup.suspects.length; _i++>><<set _s to setup.suspects[_i]>><li @class="_ok[_i] ? 'ok' : 'no'"><b><<print _s.name>>:</b> you picked “<<print _s.keys[$key[_s.id]][0]>>” and said <<print $sus[_s.id] is "out" ? "ruled out" : "can't rule out">>. <<print _s.note>></li><</for>></ul>
<p class="note">None of these men was ever charged with the Cooper hijacking.</p>
<div class="actions">[[What's known today|RealHistory]]</div>


:: RealHistory [nobar]
<h2>What's known today</h2>
<p>The beach money is still the only ransom money ever found. The geologist's sand layers showed it arrived after the 1974 dredging, and nobody has ever explained exactly how it got there.</p>
<p>Many agents believed Cooper didn't survive the jump. In 2007, the FBI agent leading the case said no experienced skydiver would have jumped on a pitch-black, rainy night in loafers and a trench coat. But no body or parachute was ever found. In 2016, after 45 years, the FBI stopped actively working the case.</p>
<p>The search hasn't stopped. Volunteer scientists are still studying the tie, and families of suspects still bring new claims. Nobody knows who he was, or whether he lived.</p>
<div class="lesson">
<h3>Your lesson as a trainee</h3>
<ul>
<li>A new clue can answer one question and raise three more.</li>
<li>Your confidence should be only as strong as your evidence.</li>
<li>Ruling a suspect out takes evidence, and so does ruling one in.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<p class="note">Leonard Palmer is a real geologist; his interview answers are written for this game, based on his findings. The agents' and reporters' words are made up. The suspects, evidence and events are real.</p>
<div class="actions">[[Finish case|CaseClosed]]</div>


:: CaseClosed [nobar]
<<include "Banner">>
<<run setup.reportResult()>>
<div class="stamp solved big">Case closed</div>
<h2>Case 001, Part 2 complete</h2>
<p>Detective rating: <b><<print $stars>> of 5</b>. Deductions: <b><<print $deductions>> of <<print setup.dedTotal>></b>.</p>
<div class="tellrocky">Go back to Rocky and type <b>done</b>.</div>
<div class="actions secondary"><<link "Play again">><<run Engine.restart()>><</link>></div>


